# Functions x/tools/cmd/deadcode reports as unreachable from cmd/ that are
# nonetheless meant to exist. One "pkg.Func" or "pkg.Type.Method" per line.
#
# Adding a line is a claim that the function is meant to be unreachable from
# every shipped binary. Anything else belongs deleted, not listed here.
#
# The roots are cmd/ only, so a package no shipped binary imports at all is
# absent from the program and never reported. The harness fakes under tests/
# need no entry here.

# Standalone constructor kept for tests and one-off clients; production code
# obtains clients from Factory.ClientForHost so they share a pooled transport.
hoclient.NewHostClient

# Reached only from the harnesses under tests/, which are not roots for this
# run, so a harness-only helper reads as unreachable by construction.
taskworker.Pool.Stats
spanner.SetClockOffsetForTesting

# The canonical GPU-mode vocabulary. Its consumer is the agreement test that
# binds the domain constants to the `enum` tag on the create body, because a
# struct tag cannot reference a constant. Production reads the tag, not this.
device.GPUModes

# Same shape, for snapshot states: the agreement test binds the SnapshotState
# constants to the `enum` tag on the entity's state field, which the console's
# drift gate reads as the published vocabulary.
device.SnapshotStates

# Same shape, for the machine-type list filters: the workload categories and CPU
# architectures are declared twice, here and in the `enum` tags, and only the
# agreement tests hold the copies together. Five Category constants and ArchArm
# have no other reader, which is exactly why deleting them on a dead-code report
# would have removed the vocabulary and left the tag unchecked.
machinetype.Categories
machinetype.Architectures

# Every registered operation verb. The agreement tests derive their cases from
# it so they cannot silently stop covering a verb added later; the requeue
# predicate reads TaskTypes instead.
operation.Verbs

# The canonical GCE error-classification vocabulary, same shape as the enum
# vocabularies above: its consumer is the agreement test binding it to the
# `enum` tag on the host error_type response field.
gce.ErrorTypes

# The @import template names admission accepts. Its consumers are the cvd
# package tests that bind the name list to the table of template bodies and
# run every expansion back through admission; the list itself is unexported.
validation.ImportTemplateNames

# Test-key factory for the cfctl auth tests. The authtest package ships in no
# binary, but it sits under cmd/, so the cmd/... roots load it and report it,
# unlike the harness fakes under tests/.
authtest.WriteKeyFile
